## 3. Checklist for Ongoing Development

| ✅ | Item | Why it matters |
|----|------|----------------|
|✔️| **Helmet** (already added) | Sets secure defaults for CSP, HSTS, X‑Frame‑Options, etc. |
|✔️| **CORS whitelist** | Prevents browsers from calling the API from malicious origins. |
|✔️| **Rate limiting** | Thwarts credential stuffing and simple DoS attacks. |
|✔️| **Body‑size limit** | Stops attackers from consuming memory with giant payloads. |
|✔️| **Input validation** (express‑validator/Joi) | Guarantees type & format, eliminates injection vectors. |
|✔️| **Sanitization** (`trim()`, `escape()`, etc.) | Removes script tags / special characters before using data. |
|✔️| **Centralized error handling** | No unhandled promises, no stack‑trace leakage. |
|✔️| **Logging (morgan + structured logger)** | Auditable trail for security incidents. |
|✔️| **Environment‑based config** (`dotenv`, `process.env`) | Keeps secrets out of the repo and enables per‑env hardening. |
|✔️| **Graceful shutdown** (listen for `SIGTERM`/`SIGINT`) | Allows Kubernetes or other orchestrators to stop the process cleanly. |
|✔️| **Dependency health** (`npm audit`, `npm-check-updates`) | Regularly patch known vulnerabilities. |
|✔️| **HTTPS enforcement** (if behind a reverse proxy, set `app.enable('trust proxy')` and redirect HTTP → HTTPS). | Prevents man‑in‑the‑middle eavesdropping. |

